/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  CASE-LOCAL OVERLAY -- ONE FIELD, and it is a statement about this flowsheet
  rather than about the substance.

  `absorber` transfers a component only when its record declares `role solute;`
  AND a Henry pair exists against the declared solvent.  The pair
  (acetone-water) IS in the curated catalogue; the ROLE is not, because
  acetone's standard record carries none -- and adding one there is a CURATION
  act, which is reserved.

  Nor SHOULD it be there, and that is the substantive point rather than a
  procedural one.  "Solute" is not a property of acetone.  In THIS unit acetone
  is what the water washes out of a hydrogen stream; three units later, in C1,
  the same acetone is the light key of a distillation and water is the
  impurity.  A field that flips meaning between two units of one flowsheet
  belongs to the case that declares the roles, not to the substance that has
  none.

  Everything else about acetone -- criticals, Antoine, Cp, formation data, the
  UNIFAC groups, the Henry pair -- comes from the standard catalogue and is
  NOT restated here.  `Database` overlays this file field-by-field over the
  standard entry (property-axiom 4), so a second copy of any of those numbers
  would be a second home for a curated value.

  Same overlay, same reason, as tutorials/steady/absorption/acetone05.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name        acetone;
role        solute;
